import Foundation

enum SCVerseTableB {
    static let entries: [SCVerse] = [
        scv("Genesis", 1, 1, 1, "In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.", "The opening sentence of the whole library.", [.praise, .hope]),
        scv("Genesis", 1, 3, 3, "And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.", "The first spoken word in the story is about light.", [.hope, .guidance]),
        scv("Genesis", 1, 27, 27, "So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.", "A line often returned to when a person feels of little worth.", [.love, .humility]),
        scv("Genesis", 1, 31, 31, "And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the morning were the sixth day.", "The verdict on creation is spoken before anything is earned.", [.praise, .thanksgiving]),
        scv("Genesis", 2, 2, 2, "And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.", "Rest appears in the story before any human ever grew tired.", [.rest]),
        scv("Genesis", 2, 18, 18, "And the LORD God said, It is not good that the man should be alone; I will make him an help meet for him.", "An early observation that solitude was not the intention.", [.love]),
        scv("Genesis", 3, 9, 9, "And the LORD God called unto Adam, and said unto him, Where art thou?", "A question asked of someone who is already hiding.", [.mercy, .doubt]),
        scv("Genesis", 9, 13, 13, "I do set my bow in the cloud, and it shall be for a token of a covenant between me and the earth.", "A sign placed in the sky where weather itself is the reminder.", [.hope, .mercy]),
        scv("Genesis", 12, 1, 1, "Now the LORD had said unto Abram, Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father's house, unto a land that I will shew thee.", "The destination is withheld; only the first step is given.", [.guidance, .fear]),
        scv("Genesis", 12, 2, 2, "And I will make of thee a great nation, and I will bless thee, and make thy name great; and thou shalt be a blessing.", "A promise made to a childless man past middle age.", [.hope, .provision]),
        scv("Genesis", 15, 1, 1, "After these things the word of the LORD came unto Abram in a vision, saying, Fear not, Abram: I am thy shield, and thy exceeding great reward.", "Spoken to a man who had just refused a king's payment.", [.fear, .hope]),
        scv("Genesis", 15, 6, 6, "And he believed in the LORD; and he counted it to him for righteousness.", "One sentence that later writers kept coming back to.", [.hope, .humility]),
        scv("Genesis", 16, 13, 13, "And she called the name of the LORD that spake unto her, Thou God seest me.", "Hagar, a runaway servant, names God from the wilderness.", [.mercy, .love]),
        scv("Genesis", 18, 14, 14, "Is any thing too hard for the LORD?", "A question put to Sarah after she laughed at the promise.", [.doubt, .hope]),
        scv("Genesis", 22, 8, 8, "And Abraham said, My son, God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering: so they went both of them together.", "Answered on the road, before Abraham could have known how.", [.provision, .endurance]),
        scv("Genesis", 28, 15, 15, "And, behold, I am with thee, and will keep thee in all places whither thou goest, and will bring thee again into this land; for I will not leave thee, until I have done that which I have spoken to thee of.", "Said to Jacob the night he ran from his brother.", [.fear, .guidance]),
        scv("Genesis", 28, 16, 16, "And Jacob awaked out of his sleep, and he said, Surely the LORD is in this place; and I knew it not.", "A man discovers, on waking, where he had been sleeping.", [.humility, .praise]),
        scv("Genesis", 32, 26, 26, "And he said, Let me go, for the day breaketh. And he said, I will not let thee go, except thou bless me.", "Jacob wrestles all night and refuses to quit at dawn.", [.endurance]),
        scv("Genesis", 50, 20, 20, "But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but God meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.", "Joseph says this to the brothers who sold him.", [.mercy, .hope]),
        scv("Exodus", 2, 24, 24, "And God heard their groaning, and God remembered his covenant with Abraham, with Isaac, and with Jacob.", "The rescue begins with listening, long before anything visibly changes.", [.mercy, .hope]),
        scv("Exodus", 3, 5, 5, "And he said, Draw not nigh hither: put off thy shoes from off thy feet, for the place whereon thou standest is holy ground.", "An ordinary hillside turns out to be something else.", [.humility]),
        scv("Exodus", 3, 12, 12, "And he said, Certainly I will be with thee; and this shall be a token unto thee, that I have sent thee: When thou hast brought forth the people out of Egypt, ye shall serve God upon this mountain.", "Moses asked who he was; the answer was about presence.", [.fear, .guidance]),
        scv("Exodus", 3, 14, 14, "And God said unto Moses, I AM THAT I AM: and he said, Thus shalt thou say unto the children of Israel, I AM hath sent me unto you.", "The name given at the burning bush resists easy definition.", [.praise, .guidance]),
        scv("Exodus", 13, 21, 21, "And the LORD went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light; to go by day and night.", "Guidance took a form they could see from anywhere in camp.", [.guidance, .hope]),
        scv("Exodus", 14, 13, 13, "And Moses said unto the people, Fear ye not, stand still, and see the salvation of the LORD, which he will shew to you to day.", "Said with an army behind them and water ahead.", [.fear, .rest]),
        scv("Exodus", 14, 14, 14, "The LORD shall fight for you, and ye shall hold your peace.", "Sometimes the assignment is to stop struggling.", [.rest, .fear]),
        scv("Exodus", 15, 2, 2, "The LORD is my strength and song, and he is become my salvation: he is my God, and I will prepare him an habitation; my father's God, and I will exalt him.", "Sung on the far shore, the morning after the escape.", [.praise, .thanksgiving]),
        scv("Exodus", 16, 4, 4, "Then said the LORD unto Moses, Behold, I will rain bread from heaven for you; and the people shall go out and gather a certain rate every day.", "Enough for the day, and no way to hoard it.", [.provision]),
        scv("Exodus", 20, 3, 3, "Thou shalt have no other gods before me.", "The first of the ten, given at Sinai.", [.guidance]),
        scv("Exodus", 20, 8, 8, "Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy.", "A command to stop, given to people newly out of slavery.", [.rest]),
        scv("Exodus", 20, 12, 12, "Honour thy father and thy mother: that thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.", "The first of the commandments that concerns other people.", [.love, .humility]),
        scv("Exodus", 33, 14, 14, "And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.", "Moses had just said he would not move without it.", [.rest, .guidance]),
        scv("Exodus", 34, 6, 6, "And the LORD passed by before him, and proclaimed, The LORD, The LORD God, merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth.", "A self-description given after the people had already failed.", [.mercy, .love]),
        scv("Leviticus", 19, 18, 18, "Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am the LORD.", "A line quoted for centuries afterward as a summary.", [.love, .mercy]),
        scv("Leviticus", 26, 12, 12, "And I will walk among you, and will be your God, and ye shall be my people.", "The promise is nearness rather than distance.", [.love, .hope]),
        scv("Numbers", 6, 24, 26, "The LORD bless thee, and keep thee: The LORD make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee: The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.", "The blessing the priests were told to say over the people.", [.hope, .rest]),
        scv("Numbers", 23, 19, 19, "God is not a man, that he should lie; neither the son of man, that he should repent: hath he said, and shall he not do it? or hath he spoken, and shall he not make it good?", "Spoken by an outsider hired to curse and unable to.", [.hope, .doubt]),
        scv("Numbers", 14, 9, 9, "Only rebel not ye against the LORD, neither fear ye the people of the land; for they are bread for us: their defence is departed from them, and the LORD is with us: fear them not.", "The minority report from two scouts among twelve.", [.fear, .endurance]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 4, 29, 29, "But if from thence thou shalt seek the LORD thy God, thou shalt find him, if thou seek him with all thy heart and with all thy soul.", "Addressed to people imagined as already far from home.", [.hope, .guidance]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 6, 4, 5, "Hear, O Israel: The LORD our God is one LORD: And thou shalt love the LORD thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might.", "The words Israel was told to repeat daily at home.", [.love, .guidance]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 8, 2, 2, "And thou shalt remember all the way which the LORD thy God led thee these forty years in the wilderness, to humble thee, and to prove thee, to know what was in thine heart.", "A backward look at years that felt like delay.", [.humility, .endurance]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 8, 3, 3, "And he humbled thee, and suffered thee to hunger, and fed thee with manna, which thou knewest not, neither did thy fathers know; that he might make thee know that man doth not live by bread only, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of the LORD doth man live.", "Hunger and provision are described in the same sentence.", [.provision, .humility]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 10, 12, 12, "And now, Israel, what doth the LORD thy God require of thee, but to fear the LORD thy God, to walk in all his ways, and to love him, and to serve the LORD thy God with all thy heart and with all thy soul.", "A summary offered near the end of Moses' life.", [.guidance, .love]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 30, 19, 19, "I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live.", "The choice is presented plainly, without pressure of argument.", [.guidance, .wisdom]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 31, 6, 6, "Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.", "Said to a generation about to cross without their leader.", [.fear, .endurance]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 31, 8, 8, "And the LORD, he it is that doth go before thee; he will be with thee, he will not fail thee, neither forsake thee: fear not, neither be dismayed.", "Moses hands the task to Joshua in public.", [.fear, .guidance]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 33, 27, 27, "The eternal God is thy refuge, and underneath are the everlasting arms.", "From Moses' final blessing over the tribes.", [.rest, .hope]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 29, 29, 29, "The secret things belong unto the LORD our God: but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever.", "A quiet limit placed on how much we will know.", [.humility, .wisdom]),
        scv("Deuteronomy", 32, 4, 4, "He is the Rock, his work is perfect: for all his ways are judgment: a God of truth and without iniquity, just and right is he.", "From the song Moses taught the people to remember.", [.praise, .justice]),
        scv("Joshua", 1, 5, 5, "There shall not any man be able to stand before thee all the days of thy life: as I was with Moses, so I will be with thee: I will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.", "Joshua inherits a job that had belonged to a legend.", [.fear, .endurance]),
        scv("Joshua", 1, 9, 9, "Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.", "Courage is given as an instruction, not a feeling.", [.fear, .endurance]),
        scv("Joshua", 24, 15, 15, "And if it seem evil unto you to serve the LORD, choose you this day whom ye will serve; but as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD.", "An old leader states his own decision and leaves theirs open.", [.guidance, .humility]),
        scv("Joshua", 23, 14, 14, "Not one thing hath failed of all the good things which the LORD your God spake concerning you; all are come to pass unto you, and not one thing hath failed thereof.", "A review offered at the end of a long life.", [.thanksgiving, .hope]),
        scv("Judges", 6, 12, 12, "And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him, and said unto him, The LORD is with thee, thou mighty man of valour.", "Gideon was hiding in a winepress when this was said.", [.fear, .hope]),
        scv("Ruth", 1, 16, 16, "And Ruth said, Intreat me not to leave thee, or to return from following after thee: for whither thou goest, I will go; and where thou lodgest, I will lodge: thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God.", "A widow chooses her mother-in-law over going home.", [.love, .endurance]),
        scv("Ruth", 2, 12, 12, "The LORD recompense thy work, and a full reward be given thee of the LORD God of Israel, under whose wings thou art come to trust.", "Boaz blesses a foreigner gleaning in his field.", [.mercy, .provision]),
        scv("Ruth", 4, 15, 15, "And he shall be unto thee a restorer of thy life, and a nourisher of thine old age: for thy daughter in law, which loveth thee, is better to thee than seven sons, hath borne him.", "The women of the town speak to Naomi at the end.", [.hope, .love]),
        scv("1 Samuel", 2, 2, 2, "There is none holy as the LORD: for there is none beside thee: neither is there any rock like our God.", "Hannah prays this after years of being unable to conceive.", [.praise]),
        scv("1 Samuel", 3, 10, 10, "And the LORD came, and stood, and called as at other times, Samuel, Samuel. Then Samuel answered, Speak; for thy servant heareth.", "A boy learns to recognize a voice he had mistaken.", [.guidance, .humility]),
        scv("1 Samuel", 12, 24, 24, "Only fear the LORD, and serve him in truth with all your heart: for consider how great things he hath done for you.", "Samuel's parting counsel after the people asked for a king.", [.guidance, .thanksgiving]),
        scv("1 Samuel", 15, 22, 22, "And Samuel said, Hath the LORD as great delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices, as in obeying the voice of the LORD? Behold, to obey is better than sacrifice, and to hearken than the fat of rams.", "A prophet distinguishes ceremony from actual listening.", [.humility, .wisdom]),
        scv("1 Samuel", 16, 7, 7, "But the LORD said unto Samuel, Look not on his countenance, or on the height of his stature; because I have refused him: for the LORD seeth not as man seeth; for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the LORD looketh on the heart.", "The prophet was about to pick the tallest brother.", [.humility, .wisdom]),
        scv("1 Samuel", 17, 47, 47, "And all this assembly shall know that the LORD saveth not with sword and spear: for the battle is the LORD's, and he will give you into our hands.", "A shepherd boy explains himself before the fight.", [.fear, .endurance]),
        scv("2 Samuel", 22, 2, 3, "And he said, The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; The God of my rock; in him will I trust: he is my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower, and my refuge, my saviour; thou savest me from violence.", "David's song looking back over years of being hunted.", [.hope, .praise]),
        scv("2 Samuel", 22, 31, 31, "As for God, his way is perfect; the word of the LORD is tried: he is a buckler to all them that trust in him.", "Tried here means tested, like metal in fire.", [.hope, .endurance]),
        scv("2 Samuel", 7, 22, 22, "Wherefore thou art great, O LORD God: for there is none like thee, neither is there any God beside thee, according to all that we have heard with our ears.", "David prays after being told not to build the temple.", [.praise, .humility]),
        scv("1 Kings", 18, 21, 21, "And Elijah came unto all the people, and said, How long halt ye between two opinions? if the LORD be God, follow him: but if Baal, then follow him. And the people answered him not a word.", "The crowd's silence is part of the scene.", [.doubt, .guidance]),
        scv("1 Kings", 19, 12, 12, "And after the earthquake a fire; but the LORD was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice.", "Elijah, exhausted and hiding, hears something quiet.", [.rest, .guidance]),
        scv("2 Kings", 6, 16, 16, "And he answered, Fear not: for they that be with us are more than they that be with them.", "Elisha's servant had just counted the enemy horses.", [.fear, .hope]),
        scv("1 Chronicles", 16, 34, 34, "O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever.", "A refrain repeated across many generations of worship.", [.thanksgiving, .mercy]),
        scv("2 Chronicles", 7, 14, 14, "If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.", "Spoken to Solomon at night after the temple was finished.", [.humility, .mercy]),
        scv("2 Chronicles", 20, 12, 12, "O our God, wilt thou not judge them? for we have no might against this great company that cometh against us; neither know we what to do: but our eyes are upon thee.", "A king admits publicly that he has no plan.", [.doubt, .fear]),
        scv("2 Chronicles", 16, 9, 9, "For the eyes of the LORD run to and fro throughout the whole earth, to shew himself strong in the behalf of them whose heart is perfect toward him.", "A rebuke to a king who trusted an alliance instead.", [.hope, .guidance]),
        scv("Nehemiah", 1, 4, 4, "And it came to pass, when I heard these words, that I sat down and wept, and mourned certain days, and fasted, and prayed before the God of heaven.", "The rebuilding project begins with several days of grief.", [.doubt, .humility]),
        scv("Nehemiah", 8, 10, 10, "Then he said unto them, Go your way, eat the fat, and drink the sweet, and send portions unto them for whom nothing is prepared: for this day is holy unto our LORD: neither be ye sorry; for the joy of the LORD is your strength.", "The people were weeping; they were told to feast and share.", [.thanksgiving, .hope]),
        scv("Nehemiah", 9, 17, 17, "But thou art a God ready to pardon, gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and forsookest them not.", "Part of a long public confession of national failure.", [.mercy, .love]),
        scv("Esther", 4, 14, 14, "For if thou altogether holdest thy peace at this time, then shall there enlargement and deliverance arise to the Jews from another place; but thou and thy father's house shall be destroyed: and who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this?", "Mordecai's message to a queen who could stay silent.", [.endurance, .justice]),
        scv("Isaiah", 1, 18, 18, "Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.", "An invitation to talk rather than a sentence handed down.", [.mercy, .hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 6, 3, 3, "And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory.", "Isaiah's vision in the year that a king died.", [.praise]),
        scv("Isaiah", 6, 8, 8, "Also I heard the voice of the Lord, saying, Whom shall I send, and who will go for us? Then said I, Here am I; send me.", "The volunteering follows immediately after being forgiven.", [.guidance, .humility]),
        scv("Isaiah", 9, 2, 2, "The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light: they that dwell in the land of the shadow of death, upon them hath the light shined.", "Written about a region that had already been overrun.", [.hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 9, 6, 6, "For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.", "Words that later became inseparable from December.", [.hope, .praise]),
        scv("Isaiah", 26, 3, 3, "Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.", "Stayed here carries the sense of leaning or resting.", [.rest, .fear]),
        scv("Isaiah", 30, 15, 15, "For thus saith the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel; In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not.", "The last four words record how the offer was received.", [.rest, .doubt]),
        scv("Isaiah", 30, 21, 21, "And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left.", "The guidance comes from behind, as you are already moving.", [.guidance]),
        scv("Isaiah", 40, 11, 11, "He shall feed his flock like a shepherd: he shall gather the lambs with his arm, and carry them in his bosom, and shall gently lead those that are with young.", "The pace is set by the slowest in the flock.", [.love, .rest]),
        scv("Isaiah", 40, 28, 28, "Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, that the everlasting God, the LORD, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary? there is no searching of his understanding.", "A question aimed at people who felt overlooked.", [.endurance, .hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 40, 29, 29, "He giveth power to the faint; and to them that have no might he increaseth strength.", "The offer is addressed specifically to the depleted.", [.endurance, .provision]),
        scv("Isaiah", 40, 31, 31, "But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.", "Written to exiles who had waited a long time already.", [.endurance, .hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 41, 10, 10, "Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.", "Four promises stacked against one instruction.", [.fear, .hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 41, 13, 13, "For I the LORD thy God will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee.", "The picture is of a hand taken, not a distant order.", [.fear, .love]),
        scv("Isaiah", 43, 1, 1, "But now thus saith the LORD that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine.", "Spoken to a defeated nation, addressed by name.", [.fear, .love]),
        scv("Isaiah", 43, 2, 2, "When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.", "Note that the water and fire are not removed.", [.fear, .endurance]),
        scv("Isaiah", 43, 19, 19, "Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.", "Said to people whose recent history was mostly loss.", [.hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 49, 15, 15, "Can a woman forget her sucking child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? yea, they may forget, yet will I not forget thee.", "Even the strongest human bond is allowed to fail here.", [.love, .mercy]),
        scv("Isaiah", 49, 16, 16, "Behold, I have graven thee upon the palms of my hands; thy walls are continually before me.", "Graven means cut in, not written down.", [.love, .hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 53, 3, 3, "He is despised and rejected of men; a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief: and we hid as it were our faces from him; he was despised, and we esteemed him not.", "The figure in this chapter is described by what he lost.", [.mercy, .humility]),
        scv("Isaiah", 53, 5, 5, "But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.", "One of the most quoted verses in the Hebrew scriptures.", [.mercy, .hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 53, 6, 6, "All we like sheep have gone astray; we have turned every one to his own way; and the LORD hath laid on him the iniquity of us all.", "The confession is plural before it is personal.", [.humility, .mercy]),
        scv("Isaiah", 54, 10, 10, "For the mountains shall depart, and the hills be removed; but my kindness shall not depart from thee, neither shall the covenant of my peace be removed, saith the LORD that hath mercy on thee.", "The comparison uses the least movable things they knew.", [.love, .hope]),
        scv("Isaiah", 55, 1, 1, "Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters, and he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price.", "A market call addressed to people who cannot pay.", [.provision, .mercy]),
        scv("Isaiah", 55, 8, 9, "For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my ways, saith the LORD. For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts.", "Offered as comfort in a passage about forgiveness.", [.humility, .wisdom]),
        scv("Isaiah", 55, 11, 11, "So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please, and it shall prosper in the thing whereto I sent it.", "The image before this is rain that has to fall somewhere.", [.hope, .endurance]),
        scv("Isaiah", 58, 11, 11, "And the LORD shall guide thee continually, and satisfy thy soul in drought, and make fat thy bones: and thou shalt be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water, whose waters fail not.", "The chapter around it is about feeding the hungry.", [.guidance, .provision]),
        scv("Isaiah", 61, 1, 1, "The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon me; because the LORD hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound.", "A commission described entirely in terms of who benefits.", [.hope, .mercy]),
        scv("Isaiah", 64, 8, 8, "But now, O LORD, thou art our father; we are the clay, and thou our potter; and we all are the work of thy hand.", "Part of a prayer that admits national failure first.", [.humility]),
        scv("Isaiah", 66, 13, 13, "As one whom his mother comforteth, so will I comfort you; and ye shall be comforted in Jerusalem.", "The comparison chosen is domestic and ordinary.", [.love, .rest]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 1, 5, 5, "Before I formed thee in the belly I knew thee; and before thou camest forth out of the womb I sanctified thee, and I ordained thee a prophet unto the nations.", "Said to a young man who felt unqualified.", [.hope, .guidance]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 1, 8, 8, "Be not afraid of their faces: for I am with thee to deliver thee, saith the LORD.", "Faces, because his audience would be hostile.", [.fear]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 6, 16, 16, "Thus saith the LORD, Stand ye in the ways, and see, and ask for the old paths, where is the good way, and walk therein, and ye shall find rest for your souls.", "Advice to stop at a crossroads and ask before choosing.", [.wisdom, .rest]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 9, 23, 24, "Thus saith the LORD, Let not the wise man glory in his wisdom, neither let the mighty man glory in his might, let not the rich man glory in his riches: But let him that glorieth glory in this, that he understandeth and knoweth me, that I am the LORD which exercise lovingkindness, judgment, and righteousness, in the earth: for in these things I delight, saith the LORD.", "Three common sources of pride, listed and set aside.", [.humility, .wisdom]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 17, 7, 8, "Blessed is the man that trusteth in the LORD, and whose hope the LORD is. For he shall be as a tree planted by the waters, and that spreadeth out her roots by the river, and shall not see when heat cometh, but her leaf shall be green; and shall not be careful in the year of drought, neither shall cease from yielding fruit.", "The tree is not spared the heat, only the withering.", [.endurance, .hope]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 29, 11, 11, "For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, saith the LORD, thoughts of peace, and not of evil, to give you an expected end.", "Sent by letter to exiles told to settle in for seventy years.", [.hope]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 29, 13, 13, "And ye shall seek me, and find me, when ye shall search for me with all your heart.", "Written to people far from the place they associated with God.", [.guidance, .hope]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 31, 3, 3, "The LORD hath appeared of old unto me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.", "Drawn, rather than driven, is the word chosen.", [.love, .mercy]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 32, 17, 17, "Ah Lord GOD! behold, thou hast made the heaven and the earth by thy great power and stretched out arm, and there is nothing too hard for thee.", "Prayed while under arrest in a city about to fall.", [.hope, .doubt]),
        scv("Jeremiah", 33, 3, 3, "Call unto me, and I will answer thee, and shew thee great and mighty things, which thou knowest not.", "Spoken to a prophet already confined in the prison court.", [.guidance, .hope]),
        scv("Ezekiel", 34, 16, 16, "I will seek that which was lost, and bring again that which was driven away, and will bind up that which was broken, and will strengthen that which was sick.", "A chapter contrasting careless shepherds with a careful one.", [.mercy, .love]),
        scv("Ezekiel", 36, 26, 26, "A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.", "The change described is internal rather than circumstantial.", [.hope, .mercy]),
        scv("Ezekiel", 37, 3, 3, "And he said unto me, Son of man, can these bones live? And I answered, O Lord GOD, thou knowest.", "An honest answer from someone who would not guess.", [.doubt, .hope]),
        scv("Daniel", 2, 20, 20, "Daniel answered and said, Blessed be the name of God for ever and ever: for wisdom and might are his.", "Praise offered in the middle of a death sentence.", [.praise, .wisdom]),
        scv("Daniel", 3, 17, 18, "If it be so, our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace, and he will deliver us out of thine hand, O king. But if not, be it known unto thee, O king, that we will not serve thy gods.", "Their resolve did not depend on the outcome.", [.endurance, .fear]),
        scv("Daniel", 6, 10, 10, "Now when Daniel knew that the writing was signed, he went into his house; and his windows being open in his chamber toward Jerusalem, he kneeled upon his knees three times a day, and prayed, and gave thanks before his God, as he did aforetime.", "The last three words are the point of the sentence.", [.endurance, .thanksgiving]),
        scv("Daniel", 6, 22, 22, "My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions' mouths, that they have not hurt me.", "Daniel's report from the bottom of the den at dawn.", [.hope, .thanksgiving]),
        scv("Daniel", 9, 9, 9, "To the Lord our God belong mercies and forgivenesses, though we have rebelled against him.", "From a prayer of confession made on behalf of a nation.", [.mercy, .humility]),
        scv("Daniel", 12, 3, 3, "And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.", "The closing vision of the book looks a long way ahead.", [.wisdom, .hope]),
        scv("Hosea", 6, 3, 3, "Then shall we know, if we follow on to know the LORD: his going forth is prepared as the morning; and he shall come unto us as the rain, as the latter and former rain unto the earth.", "Both rains named here were the ones farmers depended on.", [.hope, .guidance]),
        scv("Hosea", 6, 6, 6, "For I desired mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings.", "A short line quoted often by later teachers.", [.mercy, .humility]),
        scv("Joel", 2, 13, 13, "And rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the LORD your God: for he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repenteth him of the evil.", "Tearing clothes was the visible custom; this asks for more.", [.humility, .mercy]),
        scv("Joel", 2, 25, 25, "And I will restore to you the years that the locust hath eaten, the cankerworm, and the caterpiller, and the palmerworm, my great army which I sent among you.", "Spoken to farmers after successive waves of insects.", [.hope, .provision]),
        scv("Amos", 5, 24, 24, "But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.", "The image is a river, not a trickle.", [.justice]),
        scv("Amos", 5, 14, 14, "Seek good, and not evil, that ye may live: and so the LORD, the God of hosts, shall be with you, as ye have spoken.", "A prophet tests whether the claim matches the conduct.", [.justice, .guidance]),
        scv("Jonah", 2, 2, 2, "And said, I cried by reason of mine affliction unto the LORD, and he heard me; out of the belly of hell cried I, and thou heardest my voice.", "A prayer made from the least likely place.", [.doubt, .hope]),
        scv("Jonah", 4, 2, 2, "And he prayed unto the LORD, and said, I pray thee, O LORD, was not this my saying, when I was yet in my country? Therefore I fled unto Tarshish: for I knew that thou art a gracious God, and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repentest thee of the evil.", "Jonah is angry precisely because mercy was extended.", [.mercy, .humility]),
        scv("Micah", 6, 8, 8, "He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?", "Three requirements, stated after a list of costly offerings.", [.justice, .humility]),
        scv("Micah", 7, 7, 7, "Therefore I will look unto the LORD; I will wait for the God of my salvation: my God will hear me.", "Said in a passage describing a society falling apart.", [.endurance, .hope]),
        scv("Micah", 7, 18, 18, "Who is a God like unto thee, that pardoneth iniquity, and passeth by the transgression of the remnant of his heritage? he retaineth not his anger for ever, because he delighteth in mercy.", "The prophet's own name means something close to this question.", [.mercy, .praise]),
        scv("Nahum", 1, 7, 7, "The LORD is good, a strong hold in the day of trouble; and he knoweth them that trust in him.", "One quiet verse in a book about a falling empire.", [.hope, .fear]),
        scv("Habakkuk", 2, 3, 3, "For the vision is yet for an appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it tarry, wait for it; because it will surely come, it will not tarry.", "An answer to a prophet complaining about delay.", [.endurance, .hope]),
        scv("Habakkuk", 2, 4, 4, "Behold, his soul which is lifted up is not upright in him: but the just shall live by his faith.", "The second half of this verse shaped later argument.", [.humility, .endurance]),
        scv("Habakkuk", 3, 17, 18, "Although the fig tree shall not blossom, neither shall fruit be in the vines; the labour of the olive shall fail, and the fields shall yield no meat; the flock shall be cut off from the fold, and there shall be no herd in the stalls: Yet I will rejoice in the LORD, I will joy in the God of my salvation.", "Every source of income fails, and the sentence continues.", [.endurance, .praise]),
        scv("Zephaniah", 3, 17, 17, "The LORD thy God in the midst of thee is mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.", "An unusual picture of God as the one singing.", [.love, .rest]),
        scv("Zephaniah", 2, 3, 3, "Seek ye the LORD, all ye meek of the earth, which have wrought his judgment; seek righteousness, seek meekness: it may be ye shall be hid in the day of the LORD's anger.", "Addressed to the quiet ones rather than the powerful.", [.humility, .justice]),
        scv("Haggai", 2, 4, 4, "Yet now be strong, O Zerubbabel, saith the LORD; and be strong, O Joshua, son of Josedech, the high priest; and be strong, all ye people of the land, saith the LORD, and work: for I am with you, saith the LORD of hosts.", "Encouragement given to people rebuilding something smaller than before.", [.endurance, .hope]),
        scv("Zechariah", 4, 6, 6, "Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.", "Said to a governor short on both might and power.", [.humility, .hope]),
        scv("Zechariah", 4, 10, 10, "For who hath despised the day of small things? for they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel with those seven eyes of the LORD.", "A plummet is a builder's line, a sign of work continuing.", [.hope, .endurance]),
        scv("Zechariah", 9, 12, 12, "Turn you to the strong hold, ye prisoners of hope: I will render double unto thee.", "Prisoners of hope is an odd and memorable phrase.", [.hope]),
        scv("Malachi", 3, 6, 6, "For I am the LORD, I change not; therefore ye sons of Jacob are not consumed.", "Constancy is offered here as the reason for survival.", [.hope, .mercy]),
        scv("Malachi", 3, 10, 10, "Bring ye all the tithes into the storehouse, that there may be meat in mine house, and prove me now herewith, saith the LORD of hosts, if I will not open you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that there shall not be room enough to receive it.", "Addressed to a community that had stopped supporting the temple.", [.provision, .thanksgiving]),
        scv("Malachi", 4, 2, 2, "But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.", "The last page of the Hebrew scriptures looks toward morning.", [.hope]),
    ]
}
